From: ArchivalEra <archivalera@localhost>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH v2] hi3798mv2x: print SCR_EL3 at BL31 setup only

v2: the gicv2_distif_init() EnableGrp1 (GICD_CTLR bit 1) change is
retracted.  Board bisect on mv310 shows the kernel-side equivalent
write hangs the boot (GICD_CTLR 0x1 -> 0x3, hang in time_init), and
mv310's non-secure view of GICD_CTLR accepts bit 1 non-standardly.
The same write from EL3 is neither needed nor safe to test, so this
patch now only adds the SCR_EL3 diagnostic.

bl31_platform_setup() prints SCR_EL3.  SCR_EL3.IRQ/FIQ/EA (bits
[3:1]) decide whether IRQs and FIQs from EL1/EL2 trap to EL3; if any
is set, the kernel never sees an interrupt even though the GIC
signals it.  This is the last major unchecked suspect for the
"pending at GIC, never taken" symptom on hi3798mv310, and a single
serial line closes it.
---
 plat/hisilicon/hi3798mv2x/bl31_plat_setup.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

--- a/plat/hisilicon/hi3798mv2x/bl31_plat_setup.c
+++ b/plat/hisilicon/hi3798mv2x/bl31_plat_setup.c
@@ -112,6 +112,17 @@
 	poplar_gic_driver_init();
 	poplar_gic_init();
 
+	/*
+	 * hi3798mv310 bring-up aid: SCR_EL3 decides whether IRQs/FIQs
+	 * from EL1/EL2 trap to EL3 instead of the kernel.  Bits: [0]=NS
+	 * [1]=IRQ [2]=FIQ [3]=EA, [10]=RW.  IRQ/FIQ/EA must all read 0
+	 * for a normal hand-off.  (gicv2_distif_init is intentionally
+	 * left unmodified: the kernel-side GICD_CTLR bit1 experiment
+	 * hangs on mv310, and the same write from EL3 is not needed.)
+	 */
+	NOTICE("MV310: SCR_EL3 = 0x%llx\n",
+	       (unsigned long long)read_scr_el3());
+
 	/* Init security properties of IP blocks */
 	hisi_tzpc_sec_init();
 }
